// Fairy Dust's shipped default keymap for the command palette capability.
//
// It binds only `palette::open`, the one command Fairy Dust itself declares, so every
// consumer of `with_command_palette` gets a document whose ids the command registry
// knows. A document that names an unregistered id is rejected whole, which would leave
// the palette unopenable.
//
// `secondary-` resolves per platform: Cmd on macOS, Ctrl everywhere else. The bare keys
// Fairy Dust reserves (H home, P cube spin or fold play) are deliberately left alone, so
// nothing here shadows an example's own shortcut.
//
// An application that declares its own commands supplies its own document with
// `with_command_palette_keymap`, which replaces this one — so that document binds
// `palette::open` as well as its own ids.
{
  "bindings": [
    {
      "bindings": {
        "secondary-p": "palette::open"
      }
    }
  ]
}
